      <activity id="052dc5bb-27ef-5bce-b733-2183c3c0a1ac" activityNameId="06c77554-2483-515f-9f65-f359d6d78ae2" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Electricity, high voltage, certified electricity, at grid</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Electricity, high voltage, certified electricity, at grid
This dataset describes the transmission of high voltage electricity.; UUID:bf4f4a95-95f7-3522-a16e-4e4fcd116852
Included are the electricity production in Switzerland and from imports, the transmission network and direct emissions to air (ozone and N2O). Electricity losses are accounted for.
Location: Data apply to public and self producers. Geographical classification according to IEA. Ozone- and NO2-emission factors are based on published measurements made in various countries.  Transmission network, losses and emissions are taken from Itten, Frischknecht and Stucki (2014): LCI of Electricity Mixes and Grid.
Technology: Average technology used to transmit and distribute electricity. Includes underground and overhead lines. Electricity production according to related datasets
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: 
Sampling: Statistical data
Extrapolations: 
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_bf4f4a95-95f7-3522-a16e-4e4fcd116852.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
